
$CATEGORY: Q10 - Conditionals and logic

::Q1001:: boolean - A data type with only two possible values, true and false. {TRUE}

::Q1002:: relational operator - compares two values and produces a boolean indicating the relationship between them.{TRUE}

::Q1003:: conditional statement - A statement that uses a condition to determine which statements to execute.{TRUE}

::Q1004:: block - sequence of statements, surrounded by braces, that generally runs as the result of a condition.{TRUE}

::Q1005:: branch - one of the alternative blocks after a conditional statement.{TRUE}

::Q1006:: chaining - {
    =A way of joining several conditional statements in sequence.
    ~Putting a conditional statement inside one or both branches of another conditional statement.
}

::Q1007:: nesting - {
    ~A way of joining several conditional statements in sequence.
    =Putting a conditional statement inside one or both branches of another conditional statement.
}

::Q1008:: logical operator - combines boolean values and produces a boolean value.{TRUE}

::Q1009:: flag - variable (usually boolean) that represents a condition or status.{TRUE}

::Q1001:: validate - to confirm that an input value is of the correct type and within the expected range.{TRUE}

$CATEGORY: Q11 - Loops and strings

::Q1101::
loop - A statement that executes a sequence of statements repeatedly.{TRUE}

::Q1102::
loop body - The statements inside the loop.{TRUE}

::Q1103::
infinite loop - A loop whose condition is always true.{TRUE}

::Q1104::
iteration - Executing a sequence of statements repeatedly.{TRUE}

::Q1105::
loop variable - {
    =A variable that is initialized, tested, and updated in order to control a loop.
    ~An integer variable or value used to indicate a character in a string.
}

::Q1106::
index - {
    ~A variable that is initialized, tested, and updated in order to control a loop.
    =An integer variable or value used to indicate a character in a string.
}

::Q1107::
Unicode - An international standard for representing characters in most of the languages.{TRUE}

::Q1108::
empty string - The string which contains no characters and has a length of zero.{TRUE}

